module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Quot.CoherentStackAlgebraicUnconditional
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Quot.QuotFunctorAlgebraicFromExistence

/-!
# The Quot functor is an algebraic space, from the algebraicity of `Coh_{X/B}`

Let `f : X ⟶ B` be a morphism of algebraic spaces over a scheme `S` which is of finite
presentation and separated, and `F` a quasi-coherent `𝒪_X`-module. Stacks 09TU says that
`Quot_{F/X/B}` is an algebraic space, locally of finite presentation over `B` when `F` is of
finite presentation. This file follows the source's proof:

* the 1-morphism `Quot_{F/X/B} ⟶ Coh_{X/B}` is representable by algebraic spaces once the relative
  Hom functors `Hom(F_T, 𝒢)` are algebraic spaces
  (`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.QuotSitePresheafModel.isAlgebraicSpace_of_homRepresentations`), and
  they are, by the first assertion of Stacks 08K6
  (`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.QuotSituation.hasHomRepresentation_of_isEtaleLocallyGeneratedBelow`);
* `Coh_{X/B}` is an algebraic stack by Stacks 09DS
  (`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.CoherentSituation.isAlgebraicStack_coherentCFG`);
* the second assertion follows from the first by
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.QuotSitePresheafModel.isLocallyOfFinitePresentation_toBase`.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.QuotSituation.isAlgebraicSpace_quotSitePresheafModel_of_isSeparated`:
  every model of `Quot_{F/X/B}` is an algebraic space, for `F` étale-locally generated by fewer
  than `μ` sections with `μ` below the cutoff of the site.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.QuotSituation.isLocallyOfFinitePresentation_toBase_of_isSeparated`:
  for `F` of finite presentation every model of `Quot_{F/X/B}` is moreover locally of finite
  presentation over `B`.

Neither carries an `@[stacks]` attribute; they are the inputs of Stacks 0D01 for `F = 𝒪_X`.

## Implementation notes

**The first result is stated for `F` étale-locally generated by fewer than `μ` sections, `μ`
below the cutoff of the site.** On the size-bounded site the assertion for an arbitrary
quasi-coherent `F` fails for the reason the first assertion of Stacks 08K6 does: for
`X = B = Spec k` and `F = 𝒪^{⊕ I}` with `#I` at least the cutoff, the rank one quotients of `F`
form the projective space on `I`, whose charts `Spec k[x_i : i ∈ I]` have residue fields of
cardinality `#I`, so no étale atlas by schemes of the site exists. Every `F` of finite type
satisfies the bound
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.exists_isEtaleLocallyGeneratedBelow_lt_cutoff_of_isFiniteTypeOnSite`),
among them `𝒪_X`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 09TU](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/09TU)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 09DS](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/09DS)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 08K6](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/08K6)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits

universe u

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.Space

attribute [local instance] pointTopology

attribute [local implicit_reducible] AlgebraicGeometry.Space.QuotSituation.toCoherentSituation

variable {B : BigFppfSite.{u}} {S : Scheme.{u}} {hS : B.Contains S}

namespace QuotSituation

variable (D : QuotSituation B S hS)

/-- **Every model of `Quot_{F/X/B}` is an algebraic space** (the first assertion of Stacks 09TU,
for `F` étale-locally generated by fewer than `μ` sections with `μ` below the cutoff of the site,
for instance `F` of finite type). Here `f : X ⟶ B` is of finite presentation (a field of the
standing datum `D` of Situation 09TR) and separated. The proof is the source's: `Coh_{X/B}` is an
algebraic stack (Stacks 09DS), the relative Hom functors are algebraic spaces (Stacks 08K6), so
`Quot_{F/X/B} ⟶ Coh_{X/B}` is representable by algebraic spaces and `Quot_{F/X/B}` is an
algebraic stack in setoids, hence an algebraic space. -/
theorem isAlgebraicSpace_quotSitePresheafModel_of_isSeparated
    (hsep : IsSeparated B S hS D.f.hom)
    (hF : ∃ μ < B.cutoff, IsEtaleLocallyGeneratedBelow B S hS μ D.F)
    (N : QuotSitePresheafModel D) :
    IsAlgebraicSpace B S hS N.presheaf :=
  N.isAlgebraicSpace_of_homRepresentations.{u, u}
    (D.hasHomRepresentation_of_isEtaleLocallyGeneratedBelow hF)
    (D.toCoherentSituation.isAlgebraicStack_coherentCFG.{u, u} hsep)

/-- **Every model of `Quot_{F/X/B}` is an algebraic space locally of finite presentation over
`B`** (both assertions of Stacks 09TU for `F` of finite presentation), for `f : X ⟶ B` of finite
presentation and separated. -/
theorem isLocallyOfFinitePresentation_toBase_of_isSeparated
    (hsep : IsSeparated B S hS D.f.hom) (hF : D.F.IsFinitePresentationOnSite)
    (N : QuotSitePresheafModel D) :
    IsAlgebraicSpace B S hS N.presheaf ∧ IsLocallyOfFinitePresentation B S hS N.toBase :=
  have hN := D.isAlgebraicSpace_quotSitePresheafModel_of_isSeparated hsep
    (exists_isEtaleLocallyGeneratedBelow_lt_cutoff_of_isFiniteTypeOnSite D.X D.F
      (@SheafOfModules.isFiniteTypeOnSite_of_isFinitePresentationOnSite _ _ _ _ _ hF)) N
  ⟨hN, N.isLocallyOfFinitePresentation_toBase hN hF⟩

end QuotSituation

end AlgebraicGeometry.Space

end
